# "When the tenth +1/+1 counter is put on Shang-Chi" counts the counters it has, as a Saga's chapters do (CR 714.2b): with
# its tenth-counter trigger on the stack on turn 7, Bot1 casts Requiting Hex and blights 1, putting a -1/-1 counter on
# Shang-Chi; the state-based action takes it and one +1/+1 counter away (CR 704.5q), leaving nine. The Hex destroys Bot2's
# Ornithopter and Bot1 gains 2. Then the trigger resolves: of the five cards Bot1 draws, the first puts a tenth +1/+1
# counter on Shang-Chi again, so the ability triggers a second time - five more cards and 5 more life. Nine counters, plus
# ten from those draws: nineteen. Life: 20 + 2 + 5 + 5.

